# Timestamp conversion: encoder pts/dts are divided by the codec time base numerator (integer division) and rescaled to the
# stream time base. For integer frame rates the numerator is 1. DEFECT D-2: for 29.97 fps (time base 1001/30000) pts are
# divided by 1001, collapsing small frame indexes to 0: PES timestamps do not advance. Required behaviour: rescale without the
# division (pts counts frames).
create
world fps 60 1
start
pkt v 0 0 0 1 3000
pkt v 0 1 1 0 800
pkt v 0 2 2 0 800
pkt a 0 0 0 1 200
drain
stop 0
ts
capture_clear
world fps 30000 1001
start
pkt v 0 0 0 1 3000
pkt v 0 1 1 0 800
pkt v 0 2 2 0 800
pkt a 0 0 0 1 200
drain
stop 0
ts
